{"body":"Both parts of OWR-17469-011 are already covered by Johnston, Kabluchko and Prochno, *Projections of the uniform distribution on the cube: a large deviation perspective*, Studia Mathematica 264 (2022), 103–119, published online 17 December 2021 ([DOI 10.4064/sm210413-16-9](https://doi.org/10.4064/sm210413-16-9)). This is a correction of the source status, with full credit to the published authors.\n\nThe package matches the original random-probability-measure LDP to Theorem A, including the weak topology, speed, normalization and rate function. It also verifies that Proposition 3.1 and explicit unit-vector approximations cover the entire proposed Prohorov limit set, including boundary laws. The source audit preserves the inspected-version and access distinctions.\n\nValidation: all 527 exact normalization controls reproduce byte for byte. A separate adversarial source-match review passed both targets and added 664 exact diagnostic checks. The review and checks are included; the published theorem supplies the LDP. Only this problem’s attempt folder is changed.\n\nDisposition: already_solved in prior published literature; zero new substantive proof attempts and no campaign novelty claim.\n","headRefOid":"86be0f85c7a37a5cad8d24abd16a32d8d1f27e62","isDraft":true,"mergeCommit":null,"mergedAt":null,"number":43,"state":"OPEN"}
